<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Grand Principality of Transylvania</h1><p class="st-meta">1711 CE – 1867 CE · capital Hermannstadt; later Kolozsvár</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Habsburg crown land of Transylvania, where Hungarian, Saxon, Székely and Romanian communities contested rights until its union with Hungary in 1867.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-szatmar">Peace of Szatmár</a> in 1711 ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii-rakoczi">Francis II Rákóczi's</a> revolt, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-transylvania">Transylvania</a> was governed directly by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> as a separate land of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lands-of-the-crown-of-saint-stephen">Hungarian Crown</a>, under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopoldine-diploma">Leopoldine Diploma</a> of 1691. In 1765 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a> raised it to the rank of grand principality, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-habsburg">Habsburg</a> ruler took the title of grand prince.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A gubernium answering to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> ran the land, sitting at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sibiu">Hermannstadt</a> for much of the 18th century, with governors such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-von-brukenthal">Samuel von Brukenthal</a>. The old system of three privileged nations persisted, leaving the Romanian majority without political rights, though the union of many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanians">Romanians</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> around 1700 opened schools at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blaj">Blaj</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horea">Horea's</a> peasant revolt of 1784 was bloodily suppressed.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1848 Hungarian revolutionaries proclaimed union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanians">Romanians</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blaj">Blaj</a> demanded national rights, and civil war followed. After 1849 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-transylvania">Transylvania</a> was again a separate crown land, until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-compromise-of-1867">Compromise of 1867</a> merged it into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hungary-1526-1867">Kingdom of Hungary</a> (1867-1918). It joined <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-romania">Romania</a> in 1918.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/grand-principality-of-transylvania.jpg" alt="Grand Principality of Transylvania" width="320" height="224"><figcaption>Image: J Darnley at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Transylvania_before_1918.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1711 CE – 1867 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hermannstadt; later Kolozsvár</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Maria Theresa, Joseph II, Samuel von Brukenthal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Orthodox, Greek Catholic, Catholic and Protestant Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hungarian, Romanian, German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Transylvania (Habsburg), Grand Duchy of Transylvania</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1789&amp;focus=grand-principality-of-transylvania" aria-label="Grand Principality of Transylvania on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5265 553 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Grand Principality of Transylvania lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5381 747h0M5381 747h0M5445 768h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5585 809h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5585 809h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Romania. <a href="/atlas?year=1789&amp;focus=grand-principality-of-transylvania">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
